,"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in:\n- v4.7.dev.custom_build [bf95b6258]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev (bf95b6258) - macOS Tahoe (26.3.0) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Apple M4 Pro - Apple M4 Pro (14 threads) - 24.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen the \"Edit Animation Libraries\" window is opened, such as by selecting Animation > Manage Animations... from the Animation tab, an error like the following appears:\n```\nERROR: Couldn't find the given section \"9e3c9149c2f6404f234f0707f7f31e8d\" and key \"folding\", and no default was given.\n   at: get_value (./core/io/config_file.cpp:60)\n``` \n- I don't see any adverse effects in the editor itself; libraries are still able to be folded, and retain their fold state when the window is closed and reopened.\n- After adding a second library (in addition to the global one) to the AnimationPlayer, then closing and reopening the project, the error is no longer appearing.\n- Deleting the project's `.godot` folder, then opening the project and the \"Edit Animation Libraries\" window again caused the error to appear.\n  - I toggled the fold state of the global library, closed the window, and reopened it again; this time, the error did *not* appear.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a new project. Add an AnimationPlayer node to the scene. In the \"Animation\" tab, navigate to \"Animation > Manage Animations...\". The error should appear.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A; best seen with a completely fresh project","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.c